## Architecture and important files

- `src/synthetic_engine/{config,core,registry,engine,validation,cli}.py`: generic run
  configuration, domain protocol/registry, orchestration, inventory checks and CLI.
- `src/synthetic_engine/outputs/parquet.py`: atomic Parquet output, Zstd, hashes.
- `src/synthetic_engine/calibration/histogram.py`: reusable conditional numeric
  histograms, deterministic training/holdout split, fitting/sampling/comparison.
- `src/synthetic_engine/calibration/categorical.py`: descriptive joint category,
  weekday/hour profiling with bounded cardinality and source provenance.
- `src/synthetic_engine/domains/banking/`: banking parameters, generator, validation,
  evidence, numeric binding, payment schema and optional payment mechanisms.
- `src/synthetic_engine/domains/banking/scenarios/aml.py`: optional AML motifs and
  benign controls; separate ground truth rather than labels in feature tables.
- `specs/domains/banking/spec.md`: BANK-PAY-002 schema and BANK-PAY-003 mechanisms.
- `specs/calibration/{spec,plan,tasks}.md`: calibration requirements and open tasks.
- `docs/{calibration,adding-domains,roadmap}.md`: usage, extensions and roadmap.
- `references/banking/`: source metadata, papers, original notes and payment semantics.
- `scripts/{sample_ibm,normalize_ibm_sample}.py`: bounded exploration and normalization.

Only banking is a production domain. A non-banking test fixture verifies the
extension contract; it is not an implemented second domain. SQL/JSONL outputs,
streaming, distributed generation, resume support and a 15 GB run are not complete.

## Current behavior and limitations

Banking generates skewed account activity, relationships, timestamps, purposes,
amounts, FX assumptions and point-in-time historical features. AML supports fan-in,
fan-out, chain and cycle motifs with benign controls. AML can be disabled entirely.
No balance ledger, recurring obligations or full network calibration exists.

Numeric calibration optionally fits background principal amounts by payment
currency against IBM. It does not fit country/currency mix, timing, FX, labels,
customer segments or scenario amounts. Whole-domain `empirically_calibrated` stays
false. Row holdout is not future-time or account-disjoint validation. Previous
conditional histogram distances improved from roughly 0.22–0.29 to 0.02–0.03;
this is not a full-realism or model-performance score.

Payment schema v2 is opt-in (`payment_schema_version: 2`); v1 remains the default.
V2 adds format, raw source format, provenance, mapping status and asset class.
Source/provenance metadata is excluded from default model features. Reference
normalization preserves all seven IBM formats but does not turn reference rows
into generated engine transactions. Investment/crypto generation remains absent.

`payment_mechanisms` defaults to zero probabilities. Positive settings require v2.
- Cheque: supplier_payment, salary or personal_transfer; branch channel.
- Cash: purchase or personal_transfer; in_person channel.
- Both: same country/currency, distinct owners/accounts, unit FX, equal principal
  paid/received and assumed zero fees.
- Disjoint candidate probability intervals are filtered by eligibility; ineligible
  draws keep their original rail. Probabilities are not final population shares.
- A separate deterministic per-day RNG leaves original amounts, entities, timestamps,
  histories and AML truth unchanged. Selection does not read AML labels/motifs.
- Cash is an abstract cash-mediated transfer, NOT separate withdrawals/deposits or
  ATM activity. Cheques lack clearing delays, bounce states and balance checks.
- The default example's 0.15/0.15 probabilities are explicit assumptions, not fits.

